{
  "id": "web-dev-076",
  "title": "HTML b Tag - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>The &lt;b&gt; tag in HTML is used to make the enclosed text bold, giving it greater emphasis or visual importance.</span></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Unlike the &lt;strong&gt; tag, which also makes text bold but with semantic importance. </span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>The &lt;b&gt; tag is purely for styling purposes and does not carry semantic meaning.</span></li></ul><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span> <span class=\"na\">lang</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"en\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">meta</span> <span class=\"na\">charset</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"UTF-8\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">meta</span> <span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"viewport\"</span> <span class=\"na\">content</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>Bold Text Example<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    \n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>This is a <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">b</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>bold<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">b</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span> word in this sentence.<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Note: Alternatively, we can use the CSS </span><a href=\"#/article/web-dev/web-dev-1842\"><span>font-weight property</span></a><span> to bold text.</span></p></blockquote><h3 id=\"using-css-fontweight-property\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Using CSS font-weight Property</strong></b></h3><gfg-tabs data-mode=\"light\" data-run-ide=\"true\">\n            <gfg-tab slot=\"tab\">HTML</gfg-tab>\n<gfg-panel slot=\"panel\" data-code-lang=\"html\" data-main-code-start=\"None\" data-main-code-end=\"None\">\n    <code class=\"language-html\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"cp\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span> <span class=\"na\">lang</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"en\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">meta</span> <span class=\"na\">charset</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"UTF-8\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">meta</span> <span class=\"na\">name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"viewport\"</span> <span class=\"na\">content</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>CSS Bold Text Example<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">title</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">head</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n    \n    <span class=\"p\">&lt;</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span> <span class=\"na\">style</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s\">\"font-weight: bold\"</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>This is bold text using CSS<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">p</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">body</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"p\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"nt\">html</span><span class=\"p\">&gt;</span>\n</pre></div></code>\n</gfg-panel></gfg-tabs></div>",
  "textContent": "The <b> tag in HTML is used to make the enclosed text bold, giving it greater emphasis or visual importance.Unlike the <strong> tag, which also makes text bold but with semantic importance. The <b> tag is purely for styling purposes and does not carry semantic meaning.\n            HTML\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Bold Text Example</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n    \n    <p>This is a <b>bold</b> word in this sentence.</p>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n\nNote: Alternatively, we can use the CSS font-weight property to bold text.Using CSS font-weight Property\n            HTML\n\n    <!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>CSS Bold Text Example</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n    \n    <p style=\"font-weight: bold\">This is bold text using CSS</p>\n\n</body>\n</html>",
  "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/html/html-b-tag"
}
